export anchor BreadcrumbWebAppStyle:
    number: 216
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Breadcrumb web app
    idea: A conventional business web app with a dark top navigation bar, then a white page header with breadcrumbs, a title and its actions, then a filter bar, a sortable table and pagination, all in flat bordered boxes.
    base: light
    palette:
        navbar: #1e2733, the top navigation bar, with links in #d3dae4 and its search field in #2c3746
        navMark: #2bb3a8, the brand mark and the current link underline on the dark bar
        page: #f7f8fa, the page background below the header
        surface: #ffffff, the page header band, cards and table
        head: #f3f5f7, table heads and disabled pager buttons
        line: #dfe3e8, every box border and divider
        text: #17202b, titles and cell text
        muted: #56606d, labels, meta and uppercase heads
        primary: #0b6b66, the primary button, current page number, progress bars and the this week line
        primaryTint: #e3f2f0, the selected filter segment
        link: #0a5f91, breadcrumbs, links and the focus ring
        onTrack: #17703a, an outlined badge with a circle and tick
        atRisk: #8a5600, an outlined badge with a triangle and bang
        behind: #b3261e, an outlined badge with an octagon and cross, and overdue figures
    type:
        One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
        Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Body and cells 14px at 1.5, the page
        title 24px bold, stat values 26px bold, card titles 16px bold,
        breadcrumbs and meta 13px, and stat labels and column heads 12px
        semibold uppercase tracked 0.05em.
    layout:
        A full width dark bar 52px tall holds the brand on the left, then
        six text links with the current one white and underlined in teal,
        then a 280px dark search field with a slash key hint, a bell and
        the avatar with the name. Under it a white header band with a
        bottom border holds the breadcrumb Brightwork then Home, and a
        title row with the greeting, a meta line of the date and a red
        4 tasks are overdue, and on the right a View reports secondary
        button and a New project primary button. The body is a 1280px
        column. First a single bordered stat strip of four cells split by
        lines, each an uppercase label, a big value and a sub line. Then
        the Projects card, whose header has the title with a count pill
        and an Open Projects link, then a filter bar holding a joined
        segmented control for All 6, On track 4, At risk 1 and Behind 1
        with status glyphs, a Team select, a Sort select and a filter
        field pushed right. The table has uppercase heads, a sort arrow on
        Due, rows with the name in bold, team, a progress bar with
        percent, tasks as 9 of 10, due with days left, an outlined status
        badge and a row actions button. A footer says Showing 1 to 6 of 6
        projects beside Previous, 1 and Next buttons. Below, two cards in
        a three to two split, a line chart comparing the two weeks by
        weekday with a small values table under it, and activity as a
        vertical timeline with event icons in grey circles, linked project
        names and a Showing 6 of 6 events footer. Under 760px the links
        become a scrolling strip under the brand row, the search takes its
        own row, the segmented filter becomes two by two, each table row
        becomes a stacked block and the lower cards stack.
    spacing: A 4px base. 16px cell and card padding, 20px between boxes and a 24px page gutter.
    density: Medium. 44px table rows, 36px buttons and 32px filter controls.
    corners: 6px on every box, button, field and pager button, 4px on status badges.
    borders: 1px #dfe3e8 on all boxes and between header rows, #edf0f3 between table rows.
    shadows: None. Structure comes from borders and the dark bar.
    icons:
        16px line icons at stroke 2. Timeline events sit in 28px grey
        circles. Status glyphs are a circle with a tick, a triangle with a
        bang and an octagon with a cross. This week is a solid line with
        round dots and last week a dashed grey line with hollow squares.
    focus: A 2px #0a5f91 outline offset 2px. On the dark bar the ring is #7fd3cb. A focused field gets a blue border plus the ring.
    tone: Plain business labels in title case with uppercase column heads, such as Showing 1 to 6 of 6 projects and View reports.
